### #879 — `--restricted` composite safe mode → commented, kept open

This is the only issue this session's commits actually touched. Task 2 landed on src/cli.rs + src/help.rs, and the finding was worth reporting:

• **The flag was lying for eight days.** Its note claimed *"a dispatched `sub_agent` builds its own bash, so command execution is still one hop away (#887)"* — true on Day 188, falsified on Day 189 when #887 slice 2 made the child inherit the parent's disallow list.
• **Both surfaces corrected in one diff* (the runtime note and `--help`), because fixing one leaves two user-facing surfaces disagreeing about a confinement claim*.
• **The guard is the durable half**: `restricted_note_claims_removal_of_exactly_the_const` reads `RESTRICTED_REMOVED_TOOLS` itself, two directions, whole-token, anti-vacuous first. Positive control reddens exactly 1 test with no pre-existing test moving — which is why a false sentence shipped for eight days: nothing could fail for it.
• **Zero confinement behaviour changed.** I said that plainly rather than letting a disclosure fix read as a security fix.

Kept open because three of its five design questions stand, and the sharpest is the sibling gap in the issue body itself: file reads outside the working directory are still unbounded.

